WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.710
- It hurt a lot

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:02.923
because it was the thing I loved the most,

00:00:02.923 --> 00:00:04.872
but they were using that word

00:00:04.872 --> 00:00:07.653
and insulting me with it.

00:00:12.787 --> 00:00:16.066
Okay, so I got called a Trekkie.

00:00:17.406 --> 00:00:18.888
I guess when I was younger

00:00:18.888 --> 00:00:20.723
I didn't realize I wasn't cool,

00:00:20.723 --> 00:00:23.416
and the stuff that I was into wasn't cool.

00:00:23.416 --> 00:00:26.274
- Venom is this spiderman character

00:00:26.274 --> 00:00:28.619
that is made of black goo,

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:32.822
and he has big white eyes
and really jagged teeth.

00:00:32.822 --> 00:00:36.051
- It's probably surprising
or hard to imagine,

00:00:36.051 --> 00:00:37.769
but when I was a little kid

00:00:37.769 --> 00:00:40.583
my skin was even fairer than it is now.

00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:42.495
- My existence from the age of 11

00:00:42.495 --> 00:00:45.514
until the age of 17,
when I left high school,

00:00:45.514 --> 00:00:47.073
was miserable.

00:00:47.073 --> 00:00:48.098
- My hair was very short

00:00:48.098 --> 00:00:50.652
and I didn't have very straight teeth.

00:00:50.652 --> 00:00:53.647
So I think when people saw me

00:00:53.647 --> 00:00:55.761
I just resembled the character to them.

00:00:55.761 --> 00:00:56.925
- It was really hurtful,

00:00:56.925 --> 00:00:59.108
because I cared so much about Star Trek

00:00:59.108 --> 00:01:00.164
and thought it was so neat.

00:01:00.164 --> 00:01:04.189
And instead, it turned
into an insult, and...

00:01:05.297 --> 00:01:06.504
Yeah, it hurt a lot.

00:01:06.504 --> 00:01:08.153
- Probably the most common name

00:01:08.153 --> 00:01:09.977
that they called me was ghost.

00:01:09.977 --> 00:01:12.653
Any time there was a scary story

00:01:12.653 --> 00:01:15.328
they'd be like, "and it
was Hannah at the end."

00:01:15.328 --> 00:01:16.436
- Not only did I get called ugly

00:01:16.436 --> 00:01:19.385
but I had a bottle thrown
at my head one time.

00:01:19.385 --> 00:01:22.144
I got slammed into a door.

00:01:22.144 --> 00:01:25.678
- Started this whole
insecure downward spiral

00:01:25.678 --> 00:01:28.580
of me as a teen, going to
tanning beds all the time

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:31.715
and trying to be something I wasn't.

00:01:31.715 --> 00:01:34.060
- I did really well for myself.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.639
I got out of that town,

00:01:35.639 --> 00:01:38.101
I got a master's from Columbia

00:01:38.101 --> 00:01:39.656
on a competitive scholarship.

00:01:39.656 --> 00:01:42.910
So thanks for, I guess...

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:46.434
that shitty experience made
me into a very strong person.

00:01:48.963 --> 00:01:53.963
(uplifting music)

00:02:17.357 --> 00:02:20.027
- When it exploded it felt really good

00:02:20.027 --> 00:02:24.254
to just see it just boom up like that.

00:02:24.254 --> 00:02:27.847
- It feels like it takes
the word away from them.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:30.025
And now it can be my word.

00:02:30.025 --> 00:02:32.114
- Kind of a thing that
lingers and weighs on you.

00:02:32.114 --> 00:02:35.640
So I was not expecting to feel so happy

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.144
after doing that.

00:02:37.144 --> 00:02:40.256
But I'm overjoyed right now.

00:02:40.256 --> 00:02:41.719
- We're all in this together.

00:02:41.719 --> 00:02:44.134
We should be nice, we should
be kind to each other.

00:02:44.134 --> 00:02:47.402
And just make it as pleasant as possible

00:02:47.402 --> 00:02:48.672
while we're here.

